-- title:
--   Rationality and closedness at a crossing over O
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ over $L$ generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the function field `x1FunctionField (M * p)` of $X_1(Mp)$, let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be a nonzero element whose image in $L((q))$ is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Write $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229), glued from the spectra of the two chart algebras, with structure morphism `modelTo` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and let $X_k$ be the pullback of `modelTo` along $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$. Assume given two proper, smooth of relative dimension one, geometrically integral curves $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, together with closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ of $C_1, C_2$ into $X_k$ over $k$, such that every point of $X_k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, the scheme-theoretic intersection $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$ is reduced, and its underlying set has cardinality $n > 0$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O : A \to O$, a generator $\varpi$ of its maximal ideal, and a homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ with $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O =$ the structure map $A \to k$; put $X_O$ for the pullback of `modelTo` along $\operatorname{Spec} O \to \operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $\mathrm{bc} : X_k \to X_O$ be a morphism compatible with the first projections and with the second projections up to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$. Assume that for every point $x$ of $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$ there is a morphism $s : \operatorname{Spec}(O/\mathfrak{m}) \to X_O$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(O/\mathfrak m) \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ whose value at the closed point is the image of $x$ under $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2 \to C_1 \to X_k \to X_O$. Then for every point $\nu$ of $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$, writing $x_\nu \in X_O$ for its image under that composite, the map sending $o \in O$ to the residue at $x_\nu$ of the germ of the global section of $X_O$ obtained by pulling $o$ back along the projection $X_O \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ is a surjection onto the residue field of the stalk at $x_\nu$, and the singleton $\{x_\nu\}$ is closed in $X_O$.
--
--   This records the two point-theoretic facts attached to a crossing of the special fibre: that an $O/\mathfrak m$-valued point through $x_\nu$ forces the residue field at $x_\nu$ to be generated by the image of $O$, and that such a point of $X_O$ is closed. It is used in the construction of oriented étale crossing charts for the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $O$, where these are exactly the hypotheses required to produce a crossing chart from a crossing presentation.
